# Third-party notices

## python-pptx

This gem is a port of python-pptx (https://github.com/scanny/python-pptx).
Much of its structure, and the behaviour it reproduces, derives directly from
that project. The following files are copied from it verbatim:

    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/default.pptx
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/notes.xml
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/notesMaster.xml
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/theme.xml
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/media-speaker.png
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/docx-icon.emf
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/pptx-icon.emf
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/xlsx-icon.emf
    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/generic-icon.emf

The following file is derived from python-pptx's default template: its colour
map and text styles are taken verbatim from the slide master inside
`default.pptx`, with the shape tree emptied and the layout list cleared, so
that a master created by this gem starts from the same defaults PowerPoint
itself would use:

    lib/ruby_pptx/templates/slideMaster.xml

